    {
      "text": "There's just something about Sunday mornings. They feel different, slower, quieter, softer somehow. I woke up today without an alarm, which already felt like a win. No rush, no schedule, no reason to move fast. I made coffee, opened the window, and just stood there for a minute doing absolutely nothing, and it felt great. It's funny how Monday through Saturday, I can barely find time to breathe, but on Sundays, I suddenly notice the little things: the sound of a neighbor's radio, birds that apparently exist outside my window, even the way sunlight hits the kitchen counter. I told myself I'd be productive, maybe clean a bit, do laundry, get groceries. But yeah, none of that's happened yet. I'm still in the same spot, coffee in hand, scrolling through absolutely nothing, pretending I'm recharging. Sundays have this way of making laziness feel like self-care. And honestly, maybe it is because if the rest of the week is about doing, Sunday's the one day that's just about being.",
      "start_time": 0.119,
      "end_time": 69.3,
